Hi Sam,

So I have filled the May Welcome Center position just this morning, but I d=
o still have a Site Maintenance position available for May if you are inter=
ested in that.

As for the open Ranger positions, what will be posted is going to be the en=
try level Seasonal Ranger Assistant positions, which will not have the same=
 level of requirements as the full time Ranger positions, so generally most=
 of the Rangers, myself included, start off as Ranger Assistants that are h=
ired seasonally for the busy summer months.  It helps you to get a grasp on=
 how operations work from the park staff's side of things and helps to buil=
d those skills that are essential for getting the full time Ranger Jobs.  A=
 job that is also posted as a "Seasonal Ranger" would mean it is still on t=
he same level as a Full time Park Ranger, but they have a few months off du=
ring the calendar year, so it is still a higher-level position than a Seaso=
nal Ranger Assistant.

The Seasonal Ranger Assistant positions should be getting posted on the Wor=
kday website in the next week or so, so definitely keep an eye out for them=
.  It would be under the Parks & Recreation category, which will then list =
the Park that has posted the Seasonal Assistant Positions.

If you were to get a Ranger Assistant position it does complicate being a P=
ark Host, as you cannot do both at the same time, and would then have to fi=
nd a different place to reside as Park Staff are not given campsites to liv=
e in like the Park Hosts.  The Host site is part of the package of being a =
volunteer as it is an unpaid position, but if you were to become a paid emp=
loyee, such as a Ranger Assistant, then you will have to find your own plac=
e to reside outside of the campground.  You are still allowed to camp at th=
e campground as a paid employee, but you would be just a regular visitor at=
 that point and subject to all of the stay limits that we have for our regu=
lar guests (State Parks have a 14 day stay limit for our campers which does=
 not apply to Park Hosts).

Hopefully that adds some clarity.

[cid:image001.jpg@01DB6D89.38C31DE0]Logan Bliss | Volunteer Services Lead/R=
anger 1
