Assuming the position is still open (just perusing the job board). I'll be =
at Umpqua in April (Franki found a spot for me) so I'll still be in the are=
a.

The only caveat I would make to this is I'm going to try really hard to bec=
ome a seasonal park ranger (as long as it's on the coast), if they'll have =
me. I am unclear on when those jobs are posted and filled so I just want to=
 note this in case it causes a conflict if I am fortunately hired. Because =
of the two year park service prerequisite, I'm unsure if I would get hired =
(it is the main reason I'm volunteering).

I am open to any positions. I think I'm a very personable person so I like =
interesting with guests whether at the welcome center or as campground host=
 but I'm just as willing to clean yurts and do maintenance (I've been enjoy=
ing contributing to the infrastructure here at Tugman).

Sam

